@aizigao That is because the moment you use strings like "gpt-5" in the model's ID or name, opencode considers it a GPT-5 model and starts sending the reasoning fields. The idea is to use a name for the id/name fields that does not include the GPT characters. Here's an example of what I used:

```
      "models": {
        "do-primary": {
          "id": "do-primary",
          "name": "GPT 5.2",
          "options": {
            "model": "openai-gpt-5.2"
          }
        }
```

